racts passages related to “Uranium” and “nuclear weapons” while ColBERTv2 uses the context to extract more relevant passages associated with the discovery of atomic numbers."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_1b6aedb943798f67","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":22,"quote":"For example: \"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\" where 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the"},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_9f24a805f3d657f3","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":14,"quote":"Figure 2 (b) shows an example of instructional relevance generation, in which LLMs are instructed to output \"Yes\" if the query and passage are relevant or \"No\" if they are irrelevant."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_4e898d7f26b21f1d","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":13,"quote":"[455] address this by training models to predict the required number of hops for a given query and retrieving the relevant graph content accordingly."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_72e2b7c97301c414","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":6,"quote":"[429, 49, 212] Document Retrieval Find relevant documents related to Houston."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_bd3fae23a5267343","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":24,"quote":"These questions require integrating information across multiple passages to find relevant entities among many possible candidates, such as finding all Stanford professors who work on the neuroscience of Alzheimer’s."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_1541baa0dc5c37bd","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":15,"quote":"When using Google search, in order to avoid all pages containing the answer, we used not only the question itself as a search query, but also the entities that appear in the question as an alternative search query to obtain some pages that"},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e2936d52a59d465f","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":18,"quote":"We have observed instances where the model refuses to re-rank passages, as evidenced by responses such as \"None of the provided passages is directly relevant to the query ...\"."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_2190307acb133316","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":8,"quote":"Qualitatively, we find that the schema re- triever helps to find relevant relations that are chal- lenging for the LLMs to identify during the OIE stage."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_5501d7fc1ea7a965","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":31,"quote":"[175] utilize the off-the-shelf MedCPT retriever, a tool specifically tailored for retrieving documents in response to biomedical queries, capable of retrieving up to ten relevant pieces of evidence for each input."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_05a521270f216026","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"Retrieve the Top k chunks most relevant to the question based on semantic similarity."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_5d935a95fdca83be","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":3,"quote":"Type Input Output Definitions Retrieve x / x, y {yes, no, continue} Decides when to retrieve with R ISREL x, d {relevant, irrelevant} d provides useful information to solve x."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_726348a3e5493053","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":5,"quote":"The relevance of these passages was manually labeled as: 0 for not relevant, 1 for partially relevant, and 2 for relevant."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_fb198057dee65e19","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":21,"quote":"For each sub-sentence, they further use an LLM to retrieve the top-k most relevant relations Ri,k."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"bd72eebf611df136_c_9fecf35b54907f78","docId":"bd72eebf611df136","docTitle":"2410.05779_LightRAG_Simple_and_Fast_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":2,"quote":"By combining both detailed and conceptual retrieval, LightRAG effectively accommodates a diverse range of quries, ensuring that users receive relevant and comprehensive responses tailored to their specific needs."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_33c097996c47bb82","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":18,"quote":"Typically, a query in text format is given, such as \"What is the best way to predict a baby’s eye color?\" or \"Were there fossil fuels in the ground when humans evolved?\" [395] – the answer can be a sentence generated by a large language"},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_cc8c385b6ddbc31f","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"To further improve perfor- mance, we introduce a trained component that retrieves schema elements relevant to the input text; this improves the LLMs’ extraction per- formance in a retrieval-augmented generation- like manner."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_6f7bbe7480ca88cc","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"This is calculated by training a separate model that takes the text embedding of the query and entity as input and outputs how relevant 3Throughout this paper, we will refer to facts as triples or edges, interchangeably 19 the entity is to"},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_532122fabeccc90e","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":31,"quote":"This approach involves retrieving relevant entities and the relationships between them from an external knowledge source and structuring this information as a cohesive input for the LLM."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_3f7fee483c85589e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"To further improve performance, the three steps above can be followed by an additional Refine- ment phase: we repeat EDC but provide the pre- viously extracted triplets and a relevant part of the schema in the prompt during the initial"},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_a3afbe5e19462e1a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":20,"quote":"The indexing stage is shown in Figure 4, showing both the OpenIE procedure as well as the relevant subgraph of our KG."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_5a59c3b07af14c98","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":24,"quote":"Interestingly enough, IRCoT uses its parametric knowledge to guess that Venetoclax, which also treats leukemia, would do so through the relevant mechanism even though no passage in the curated dataset explicitly stated this."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_ff1814eb2a0b5efa","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"Re-ranking the retrieved information to relocate the most relevant content to the edges of the prompt is a key strategy."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_ff1814eb2a0b5efa","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"Once relevant context is retrieved, it’s crucial to integrate it effectively with the query."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_1b6aedb943798f67","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":22,"quote":"Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_f8159e0305a9faa2","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":43,"quote":"It is particularly useful for retrieving relevant instances within tabular data."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_384c7b091b62ac3f","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":1,"quote":"Answering a question then essentially involves retrieving relevant pas- sages from a corpus and feeding these passages, along with the original question, to the LM."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_c7b8924c28c2d6cd","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":7,"quote":"In KG as the information is stored in the form of entities and relationships and there can be multiple relations emanating from one single entity, in this experiment, to extract relevant information from th"},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_2329f3b46cbb2b36","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":3,"quote":"The hippocampus then leverages its context-dependent memory system, thought to be implemented through a densely connected network of neurons in the CA3 sub-region [76], to identify complete and relevant memories within the hippocampal"},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_f1a615fbeb84f3af","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":17,"quote":"This aspect indicates whether the evidence provides useful information (Relevant) or not (Irrelevant)."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_c80149a827872cde","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"PPR enables HippoRAG to explore KG paths and identify relevant subgraphs, essentially performing multi-hop reasoning in a single retrieval step."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f33fa415394a91f4","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":1,"quote":"To overcome challenges, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances LLMs by retrieving relevant document chunks from external knowledge base through semantic similarity calcu- lation."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_b44143332fc03b52","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":4,"quote":"(vi) Signal retrieves relevant tweets for a given news title."},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_795da409fe24f385","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":